                    "message": "Any temporary directory is fine for me \u2014 please feel free to suggest one.\n\nI need to copy pwquality.conf to a temporary directory so it can later be read by the phosphor-user-manager.bb recipe.\n\nThe reason for copying it is this:\nIf I try to reference the config file directly via an absolute path like /etc/security/pwquality.conf in phosphor-user-manager.bb, BitBake ends up resolving that path to:\n\ntmp/work/cortexa15t2hf-neon-openbmc-linux-gnueabi/libpwquality/1.4.5/git/src/pwquality.conf\n\nHowever, my actual requirement is to read the version of pwquality.conf located in the meta-layer:\n\nmeta-phosphor/recipes-extended/libpwquality/libpwquality/pwquality.conf\n\nTo achieve this, I\u2019m copying the file to a temp location during the build so that it can be accessed in a controlled and predictable way."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-phosphor/recipes-extended/libpwquality/libpwquality_%.bbappend",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Chandra Harkude",
                        "email": "Chandramohan.harkude@gmail.com",
                        "username": "chandramohan83"
                    },
                    "message": "@patrick@stwcx.xyz Please complete the review"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-phosphor/recipes-extended/libpwquality/libpwquality_%.bbappend",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Milton D. Miller II",
                        "email": "mdmii@outlook.com",
                        "username": "mdmillerii"
                    },
                    "message": "is this what you are trying to accomplish?\n\nhttps://docs.yoctoproject.org/dev/dev-manual/new-recipe.html#sharing-files-between-recipes\n\n\nplease don't mark others comments resolved until action has been taken."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-phosphor/recipes-extended/libpwquality/libpwquality_%.bbappend",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Chandra Harkude",
                        "email": "Chandramohan.harkude@gmail.com",
                        "username": "chandramohan83"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes, I am sharing config file between the recipes\n\nReplaced ${TOPDIR} with ${datadir} as suggested in https://docs.yoctoproject.org/dev/dev-manual/new-recipe.html#sharing-files-between-recipes to use  SYSROOT_DIRS"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-phosphor/recipes-phosphor/users/phosphor-user-manager_git.bb",
                    "line": 99,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Why would a config file from one repository become a build directive to another one?  Why wouldn't we load the config file in phosphor-user-manager to get a baseline?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-phosphor/recipes-phosphor/users/phosphor-user-manager_git.bb",
                    "line": 99,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Chandra Harkude",
                        "email": "Chandramohan.harkude@gmail.com",
                        "username": "chandramohan83"
                    },
                    "message": "The goal is to preserve the image build configuration. Loading the config file at runtime in phosphor-user-manager would not provide access to build-time values. (These values can be modified by PATCH requests)"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-phosphor/recipes-phosphor/users/phosphor-user-manager_git.bb",
                    "line": 99,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Chandra Harkude",
                        "email": "Chandramohan.harkude@gmail.com",
                        "username": "chandramohan83"
                    },
                    "message": "@patrick@stwcx.xyz"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-phosphor/recipes-phosphor/users/phosphor-user-manager_git.bb",
                    "line": 99,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Milton D. Miller II",
                        "email": "mdmii@outlook.com",
                        "username": "mdmillerii"
                    },
                    "message": "this sounds like you are trying to enforce some design that isn't stated.\n\nWhy should the build override the config file?\n\n\nIs the quality in the config file at runtime not being enforced on charge?\n\nDoes this result differ for administratively set vs user password change?  \n\nI'm guessing that since the file is in `/etc`, the built file is being copied into the the rwfs overlay when patched and it's not cleared via selected preservation or you aren't using same.\n\nIs there a related patch to use this configuration?\nhttps://github.com/search?q=repo%3Aopenbmc%2Fphosphor-user-manager%20MIN_PASSWORD_LENGTH&type=code"
                }
            ],
